WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
Only about 2.5 per cent
of Earth's water is fresh.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:09.710
And of that fresh water, rivers
hold about 0.006 per cent.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.870
A tiny store.

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.950
Yet through weeks without rain,
many rivers keep on flowing.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.750
How?

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.570
Does it rain somewhere
in the basin every day?

7
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.230
Does sea water flow back up the river?

8
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.390
In this mission, you'll draw a
drainage basin as an open system,

9
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.210
from the rain that falls
to the river's mouth.

10
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.930
Then you'll balance the budget of the
River Lambourn in southern England:

11
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.910
768 millimetres of rain a year on average,

12
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.470
but only 235 leaves as runoff.

13
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.240
Your mission: explain how a river keeps
flowing through weeks without rain.
